<!-- ⚠ FABRICATED — this component does NOT exist in madvib/Ship@job/sui-framework. Hallucinated during a session that ran before real source was imported. Treat as a rough sketch only; see ./README.md for triage (drop / kind-of-X / possible real gap). -->
<!--
  sui-theme-toggle.before.sui — fabricated sketch (not in source). A bare two-up segmented
  control (Light / Dark) backed by native radios — bordered box, the active
  segment gets a muted fill. Interactive via :has(input:checked), no controller.
  Compiled as <x-theme-toggle-before>.
-->
<style>
  :host { display: inline-block; font-family: var(--font-body); }
  .seg { display: inline-flex; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); overflow: hidden; }
  label { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; padding: 5px 14px; font-size: var(--text-sm); color: var(--muted-foreground); cursor: pointer; }
  label + label { border-left: 1px solid var(--border); }
  input { position: absolute; opacity: 0; width: 0; height: 0; }
  label:has(input:checked) { background: var(--muted); color: var(--foreground); }
</style>
<div class="seg" part="toggle" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Theme">
  <label><input type="radio" name="tt-before" checked />Light</label>
  <label><input type="radio" name="tt-before" />Dark</label>
</div>
